  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "ks_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -344
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Keyboard Synth\n\nPlay the computer keyboard like a piano: A S D F G H J K are the white keys from C, W E T Y U the black ones; Z / X shift an octave. Move the mouse up and down over the preview to open and close the filter. Flip Arp on and hold a chord: the arpeggiator steps through the held notes at Arp speed.\n\nHow it works: Keyboard in `keys` mode reports which of its 13 keys are held (`down`) and the latest press (`index`). Played alone, the latest key is the note and a new press dips the gate for a frame so it re-attacks; with Arp on, the held keys are filtered into a list and a clock walks it. Two MonoSynths (one an octave down) → Mix → filter → delay → reverb. Tip: press Focus on the preview so the editor doesn't also catch the keys.",
        "width": 470,
        "height": 280
      }
    },
